From b7cb5ccd2d3694a2ebf85d5f95138caf1616ce2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:38:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sequence-parallel Engram prefill column exchange and sliced
 projection

Under sequence-parallel prefill (sp_rows is not None) on a disk-sharded Engram
layer with a column-parallel wkv projection (_PaddedColumnParallelLinear),
exchange each rank's gathered hash columns by row block (interleaved_sp_rows)
so each rank interleaves, casts to MXFP8 once, and projects only its real_rows
local tokens through the gathered wkv column blocks (local_sp_product) into
[N, L, C] without a second collective after wkv.

When wkv SP shards are not gathered or the table is row-sharded across ranks,
slice wkv across ENGRAM_SLICE_TOKENS=2048 token slices via
SPRows.project_exchange_rows, writing each rank's local row block in place
while overlapping peer PyNCCL row exchanges, RankOrderParts reduction, and
pad-row mHC post / copy_columns. Replicated wkv projections under SP slice the
input rows to the rank's real_rows before projecting.

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 (patch head c47b54ae471a)
Quality: bit-identical to full-row Engram forward across TP3 and TP4; no dtype,
quantization, or accumulation order change; decode (sp_rows is None) is
unchanged.
Tests: tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py,
tests/models/test_deepseek_v41_sp_project_reduce_scatter.py, and
tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py.
Upstream status: local DeepSeek V4.1 sequence-parallel prefill optimization.
